On Friday, June 17, 2016 at 5:31:57 PM UTC-4, Krzysztof Sakrejda wrote:
> Is there some way to produce a directory of the .stan files that rstanarm uses? Do they live somewhere outside of the package?

They live in the exec/ directory

https://github.com/stan-dev/rstanarm/tree/master/exec

but utilize the #include mechanism a lot. You could do

sapply(rstanarm:::stanmodels, FUN = function(m) {
  cat(m@model_code, file = paste0("/tmp/", m@model_name, ".stan"), sep = "\n")
  invisible(NULL)
})

to write Stan files into /tmp after the #include lines have been resolved.

Ben

