From u1fe638ac9008754d at groups.google.com  Wed Jun 22 00:02:55 2016
From: u1fe638ac9008754d at groups.google.com (Ben Lambert)
Date: Wed, 22 Jun 2016 00:02:55 +0000
Subject: Re: [stan-users] Cauchy equivalent of Von Mises distribution in Stan
Message-ID: <4RYrr5lG6P4.WII8l2HEAQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <4RYrr5lG6P4._fgtaXVvBgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <4RYrr5lG6P4._fgtaXVvBgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/4RYrr5lG6P4/m/WII8l2HEAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thanks very much! Really appreciated. In case anyone else needs it, the following worked perfectly for us!

data{
  int N;
  real phi[N];
}

parameters {

  real<lower=0> kappa[N];
  real<lower=0> a;
  real<lower=0> b;
}

model{
    for (i in 1:N){
      if (kappa[i] < 100){
        phi[i] ~ von_mises(0,kappa[i]);
      } else{
        phi[i] ~ normal(0,sqrt(1/kappa[i]));
      }
        kappa[i] ~ gamma(a,b);
    }
    a ~ gamma(2,1);
    b ~ gamma(2,1);
}

