On Tuesday, June 21, 2016 at 6:30:30 PM UTC-4, Alireza RG wrote:
> Here's the model I'm trying to create:
>
> zt ∼NB(μt, k),   μt =Xb + φμt−1 +αzt−1 +(1−φ−α)μ
>
> where X is my design matrix, b is fixed effect, k is shape, α, φ, μ are positive, and  α + φ < 1.

You need to constrain the parameters such that alpha + phi < 1. So, this

> parameters {
>   real b;
>   real<lower=0> shape;
>   real<lower=0> mu;
>   real<lower=0> alpha;
>   real<lower=0> tmp;
> }

needs to become

parameters {
  real b;
  real<lower=0> shape;
  real<lower=0> mu;

  real<lower=0, upper = 1> alpha;
  real<lower=0, upper = 1 - alpha> phi;
}

which does not have the tmp variable. Then you can push what you had for transformed parameters into the model block

model {
  vector[N] eta;
  real lambda;
  eta[1] <- log(Y[1]); // log(Y[1]) could be calculated in transformed data
  lambda <- 1 - alpha - phi;

  for (t in 2:N)

    eta[t] <- X[t] * b + lambda * mu + phi * eta[t - 1] + alpha * Y[t - 1];
  Y ~ neg_binomial_2_log(eta, shape); // this should really be excluding Y[1]
  alpha ~ normal(0.5, 0.5);
  // don't use a gamma(0.01, 0.01) prior for shape
}

Ben

