> And to be more specific, I'm writing my own HMC code to sample from posterior of parameters. I leave log-likelihood and gradient calculations to Stan. As I have more than 300 parameters in my model, tuning epsilon and L is very challenging. It would be great if I could also get tuned epsilon and L from Stan.
>
>
> On Saturday, June 25, 2016 at 10:26:15 AM UTC-7, sepehr akhavan wrote:
> I'm using rstan.
>
> On Saturday, June 25, 2016 at 10:16:43 AM UTC-7, Michael Betancourt wrote:
