On Monday, June 27, 2016 at 11:35:16 PM UTC-4, Stefano wrote:
> I am aware that Stan includes a vonMises sampling statement y ~ von_mises(mu, kappa). Is this adaptable to a Multi-dimensional sphere? i.e. Mises-Fisher generalization?

No, but with Stan version 2.10.x it is easy to implement the log-PDF yourself in the Stan language, provided that either kappa is fixed or the sphere has an even number of dimensions. You just need to declare mu as a unit_vector[p] in the parameters block. If p is odd, you have to evaluate the Bessel function for a half-integer yourself.

Ben

