I predict it will work fine (evantually).

> If there are the basis, for creating the distribution myself I imagine I have to plug (which is not gonna be really straightforward :) ), is this the right route?

The LaTeX didn't really come through, but it is just the logarithm of

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Mises%E2%80%93Fisher_distribution

so you have --- for even p ---

data {
  int<lower=2> p;
  unit_vector[p] x;
}
transformed data {
  int<lower=0> half_pm1;
  half_pm1 = p / 2 - 1; // ignore integer division warning since p is even
}
parameters{
  unit_vector[p] mu;
  real<lower=0> kappa;
}
model {
  target += kappa * dot_product(mu, x) + half_pm1 * log(kappa) - log(modified_bessel_first_kind(half_pm1, kappa));
  ...
}

For odd p, you have to reimplement that Bessel function for half-integers.

Ben

