Okay, I have been thinking about this and I have a few questions, if that's okay.

1. In terms of reformulating the model to be in terms of logit(p), I have a large number of trials in which p=1, and logit(p) = inf.  Do you have any suggestions about how I should handle those trials?  There are many of them, and I would prefer to not exclude them.

2. For k[i] ~ binomial_logit(N[i], logit_p_obs[i]), what is N[i]?  I couldn't find this in the manual/documentation.  Does it correspond to that particular trial number?  Or the total number of trials?

Thank you so much!
